<title>USA: AMCON Distributing Q2 profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>AMCON Distributing Q2 profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA, Nebraska 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr profit	$0.05	     loss $0.04</p>
<p> Net profit	131		 loss 93,871</p>
<p> Sales	     40,020		   39,509</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  2,451		    2,462</p>
<p>	  6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $0.45   profit	 $0.08</p>
<p> Net profit		 1,108   profit	   206</p>
<p> Sales		     81,395		   80,775</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   2,450		    2,464</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full company name is AMCON Distributing Co.</p>
<p>The company said improved operating performance for the second quarter and six months ended March 31 mainly reflected its October 1996 sale of Denver beer distributorship. The sale enabled it to eliminate the expense of operating the facility and reduce debt, resulting in a reduction in interest expense, it said.</p>
<p>The company also said it was able to generate an after-tax gain on sale of the assets for about $500,000.</p>
